{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ES2022",
    "moduleResolution": "Bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2022"],
    "types": ["@cloudflare/workers-types"],
    "strict": true,
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["src/*"]
    }
  },
  /**
   * `src` only. Tests import from `bun:test`, whose global types conflict with
   * @cloudflare/workers-types (both declare fetch, Request, Response). Tests
   * are type-checked by `bun test`, which runs them through the same compiler.
   */
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  /**
   * Phase 6a removed the D1 binding, so `Env` no longer has `DB`. These files
   * are the ones that used it. They are finished, tested work being kept for
   * Phase 10 -- excluded from type-checking rather than deleted, so the shipped
   * surface can be genuinely database-free without throwing that work away.
   *
   * The list is the *transitive* set, which is bigger than it first looks:
   *
   *  - `projectDetail` reads the crew roster and expenses. Phase 7b brings it
   *    back with an explicit "inputs unavailable" path instead.
   *  - `invoices` reads brand settings through `readBrand`, so the print route
   *    is D1-backed even though invoices themselves are pure ERPNext.
   *
   * Everything else that is unmounted -- payables, clients, tasks, dashboard,
   * vendors, equipment, inventory, insights, lookups, customers -- is pure
   * ERPNext and stays type-checked, so it cannot rot while it waits. So do the
   * tested pure-logic libs, including `invoiceHtml`, `payQr` and
   * `invoiceNumber`: only the routes that touch storage are dropped.
   */
  "exclude": [
    "src/db/client.ts",
    "src/db/schema.ts",
    "src/lib/backup.ts",
    "src/routes/brand.ts",
    "src/routes/invoices.ts",
    "src/routes/projectCrew.ts",
    "src/routes/projectDetail.ts",
    "src/routes/projectExpenses.ts",
    "src/routes/studioRental.ts",
    "src/routes/subscriptions.ts",
    "src/routes/transactions.ts"
  ]
}
